# Response headers for the static assets Workers serves beside the api-worker (the assets binding in
# apps/api-worker/wrangler.jsonc, with single-page-application fallback). Rules match the request
# path, so the fallback document served for a route under /join/ carries them too.
#
# No cache lifetime for /_app/ belongs here. A rule keyed on the path also applies to the fallback
# document served for a file that is missing, so a long lifetime would let a browser keep HTML under
# a script's address. The lifetime is set in apps/web-worker/src/answer-application-file.ts, which
# answers a missing file with 404 first.
#
# A guest arrives at /join/<token>, where the token is a bearer credential. The page itself sets a
# no-referrer meta tag and every guest fetch sends referrerPolicy: "no-referrer", but the document's
# own script and stylesheet requests go out before either takes effect, and a Referer carrying the
# path would carry the secret into the platform's request logs. The header closes that window.
/join/*
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
